==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|rogen}} and {{m|gmh|roge}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|rogan}}, {{m|goh|rogin}}, {{m|goh|*hrogan}} and {{m|goh|rogo||roe}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*hrugnaz}} and {{m|gem-pro|*hrugô||roe}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*krek-||frogspawn}}. Compare Low German {{m|nds|Rögen}}, Dutch {{m|nl|roge}}, English {{m|en|roe}}, Danish {{m|da|rogn}}. More at {{l|en|roe}}.

